            <ArticleTitle>Quadruple Stimuli-Responsive Mechanized Silica Nanoparticles: A Promising Multifunctional Nanomaterial for Diverse Applications.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>15041-15045</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1002/chem.201704245</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Novel quadruple stimuli-responsive mechanized silica nanoparticles were constructed by installation of supramolecular nanovalves onto the exterior surface of mesoporous silica nanoparticles. The release of cargo molecules is triggered by acid/Zn2+ /alkali/reduction potential stimuli. This has potential application in the development of drug delivery systems or construction of smart anticorrosion coatings.</AbstractText>
